<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     Quick Start Modal (shown on first visit)
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="qs-overlay" id="qs-overlay" style="display:none">
  <div class="qs-modal">
    <div class="qs-header">
      <h2>🚀 Welcome to PPMF</h2>
      <p>Power Platform Monitoring Framework — Quick Start Guide</p>
    </div>
    <div class="qs-body">
      <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:16px">
        Complete these steps after importing the solution to get alerts flowing to Teams.
      </p>
      <div class="qs-steps">
        <div class="qs-step">
          <div class="qs-num">1</div>
          <div>
            <div class="qs-step-title">Assign connection references</div>
            <div class="qs-step-desc">Go to Solutions → Power Platform Monitoring Framework → Connection References. Assign a Dataverse connection to <code>ppmf_DataverseConnectionReference</code> and a Microsoft Teams connection to <code>ppmf_TeamsConnectionReference</code>.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="qs-step">
          <div class="qs-num">2</div>
          <div>
            <div class="qs-step-title">Activate child flows</div>
            <div class="qs-step-desc">All four <strong>PPMF-Child-*</strong> flows must be set to Active before error handling will work: <em>ProcessFlowError</em>, <em>FlowErrorHandler-JSON</em>, <em>FlowErrorHandler-Parameters</em>, and <em>FlowWritetoIntakeList</em>. Turn them on from the Solutions flow list. If you are using canvas app error handling, also activate <em>PPMF-Power-Apps-Error-Handler-JSON</em>.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="qs-step">
          <div class="qs-num">3</div>
          <div>
            <div class="qs-step-title">Configure environment variables</div>
            <div class="qs-step-desc">Open <strong>Configuration → Setup &amp; Configuration</strong> and set the four required variables:
              <ul style="margin:6px 0 0 16px;line-height:1.9">
                <li><strong>Environment Name</strong> — short label for this environment (e.g. <em>Production</em>)</li>
                <li><strong>Portal Base URL</strong> — use the preset button for your cloud: <em>Commercial</em> (<code>make.powerautomate.com</code>), <em>GCC High</em> (<code>make.powerautomate.appsplatform.us</code>), or <em>DoD</em> (<code>make.powerautomate.appsplatform.mil</code>)</li>
                <li><strong>Teams Group ID</strong> — the Azure AD group GUID of your target Teams team</li>
                <li><strong>Flow Alerts Channel ID</strong> — the internal channel ID (starts with <code>19:</code>) for the default alerts channel</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="qs-step">
          <div class="qs-num">4</div>
          <div>
            <div class="qs-step-title">Run the deployment checklist</div>
            <div class="qs-step-desc">Open <strong>Configuration → Setup &amp; Configuration</strong>. The page automatically runs 8 checks on load and displays a pass / warn / fail result for each. Click <strong>↻ Re-validate</strong> at any time to re-run. All 8 checks must show green before PPMF will reliably capture and alert on errors. Any red (fail) result must be resolved; amber (warn) results indicate degraded functionality.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="qs-step">
          <div class="qs-num">5</div>
          <div>
            <div class="qs-step-title">Run the demo flow</div>
            <div class="qs-step-desc">Trigger <strong>PPMF-Demo-Flow-Failure</strong> manually with a test solution name. Confirm an alert card arrives in Teams and an error record appears in the Triage view.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="qs-footer">
      <label>
        <input type="checkbox" id="qs-dont-show"> Don't show again
      </label>
      <button class="btn btn-primary" onclick="closeQuickStart()">Get Started →</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

