  <main class="app-main" id="main-content">

    <!-- ── Overview ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="card doc-section" id="overview">
      <div class="card-header">
        <span class="card-header-icon">🔍</span>
        <div>
          <div class="card-title">Overview</div>
          <div class="card-subtitle">What PPMF is and what it does</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card-body prose">
        <p>The <strong>Power Platform Monitoring Framework (PPMF)</strong> is a Dataverse-backed solution that provides automated error capture, Teams alerting, and triage management for Power Automate cloud flows and Power Apps canvas applications.</p>
        <p>When a monitored flow fails, PPMF captures structured error data to Dataverse, sends a formatted adaptive card to a Microsoft Teams channel, and creates a trackable error record for structured triage. Canvas app errors are handled through a separate entry point that accepts a JSON error payload directly from the app.</p>
        <p>PPMF is designed for enterprise deployment in <strong>Commercial</strong>, <strong>GCC High</strong>, and <strong>DoD</strong> cloud environments and is compatible with managed solution distribution.</p>

        <div class="callout callout-info" style="margin-top:8px">
          <span class="callout-icon">ℹ️</span>
          <div>PPMF requires a Dataverse connection and a Microsoft Teams connection. Both must be assigned to their connection references before any flows will process errors.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Architecture ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="card doc-section" id="architecture">
      <div class="card-header">
        <span class="card-header-icon">🏗️</span>
        <div>
          <div class="card-title">Architecture</div>
          <div class="card-subtitle">How errors flow through the framework</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card-body">
        <p class="prose" style="margin-bottom:16px"><strong>Flow error path</strong> — a monitored flow's catch scope calls the child flows in sequence:</p>
        <div class="flow-diagram">
          <div class="flow-node">
            <span class="flow-node-icon">⚡</span>
            <div>
              <div class="flow-node-name">Your flow (Catch scope)</div>
              <div class="flow-node-desc">Calls PPMF-Child-ProcessFlowError with SolutionName, workflow() JSON, and result() JSON</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
          <div class="flow-node">
            <span class="flow-node-icon">🔄</span>
            <div>
              <div class="flow-node-name">PPMF-Child-ProcessFlowError</div>
              <div class="flow-node-desc">Parses workflow context, extracts flow name + run ID, constructs portal deep link URL</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
          <div class="flow-node">
            <span class="flow-node-icon">🔄</span>
            <div>
              <div class="flow-node-name">PPMF-Child-FlowErrorHandler-JSON</div>
              <div class="flow-node-desc">Looks up alert route, checks throttle window, calls WriteToIntakeList, posts Teams card if not throttled</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
          <div class="flow-node">
            <span class="flow-node-icon">💾</span>
            <div>
              <div class="flow-node-name">PPMF-Child-FlowWritetoIntakeList</div>
              <div class="flow-node-desc">Creates ppmf_errorevent record in Dataverse (always runs — every failure is logged)</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
          <div class="flow-node">
            <span class="flow-node-icon">💬</span>
            <div>
              <div class="flow-node-name">Teams Alert Card</div>
              <div class="flow-node-desc">Posted to the matched alert route channel, or to the default channel from env vars</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="prose" style="margin-top:16px"><strong>Canvas app error path</strong> — the app calls <strong>PPMF-Power-Apps-Error-Handler-JSON</strong> directly via PowerAppV2 trigger, passing a JSON payload. The flow parses the payload, performs an alert route lookup, checks the throttle window, conditionally posts a Teams adaptive card, and always calls <strong>PPMF-Child-FlowWritetoIntakeList</strong> to write a <code>ppmf_errorevent</code> record to Dataverse. Unlike the flow error path, the Teams card is posted to the default channel from the environment variables (<code>ppmf_TeamID</code> / <code>ppmf_FlowAlertsChannelID</code>) regardless of any matching alert route — per-solution channel routing is not applied to canvas app alerts.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Post-Import Checklist ──────────────────────────────────────────── -->
