    <!-- ── Integrating Your Flows ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="card doc-section" id="integration">
      <div class="card-header">
        <span class="card-header-icon">🔧</span>
        <div>
          <div class="card-title">Integrating Your Flows</div>
          <div class="card-subtitle">How to add PPMF error handling to any Power Automate flow</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card-body prose">
        <p>Wrap all functional actions in a <strong>Try scope</strong>. Add a <strong>Catch scope</strong> configured to run after Try with status <em>Failed</em> or <em>TimedOut</em>. Inside the Catch scope, add a <strong>Run a Child Flow</strong> action:</p>

        <div style="margin:12px 0">
          <strong style="font-size:12px">Child flow:</strong> <code>PPMF-Child-ProcessFlowError</code><br><br>
          <strong style="font-size:12px">Inputs:</strong>
          <div class="code-block" style="margin-top:6px">
<span class="kw">SolutionName</span>     → <span class="str">"YourSolutionUniqueName"</span>   <span class="cmt">// free text — used for alert route matching</span>
<span class="kw">ParentWorkFlowJson</span> → <span class="fn">string</span>(<span class="fn">workflow</span>())            <span class="cmt">// captures flow name, run ID, environment</span>
<span class="kw">TryResultsJson</span>     → <span class="fn">string</span>(<span class="fn">result</span>(<span class="str">'Try'</span>))         <span class="cmt">// captures error details from failed actions</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="callout callout-tip">
          <span class="callout-icon">✅</span>
          <div><strong>SolutionName convention:</strong> use the solution's unique name (logical name), e.g. <code>PowerPlatformMonitoringFramework</code>. Avoid spaces. The string is matched by exact equality against Alert Route patterns — choose it deliberately and document it so route patterns stay consistent across your team.</div>
        </div>

        <p style="margin-top:12px">The child flow handles everything else: parsing the error, creating the Dataverse record, resolving the alert route, applying throttle logic, and posting the Teams card. You do not need to add any additional error handling logic.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

