    <!-- ── Alert Throttling ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="card doc-section" id="throttle">
      <div class="card-header">
        <span class="card-header-icon">🔇</span>
        <div>
          <div class="card-title">Alert Throttling</div>
          <div class="card-subtitle">Prevents Teams channel flooding from repeatedly failing flows</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card-body prose">
        <p>When a flow failure arrives, the error handler computes a throttle cutoff timestamp as <em>current time minus ppmf_AlertThrottleMinutes</em>. It then queries <code>ppmf_errorevent</code> for existing records where the flow name matches, the record was created after the cutoff, and the flow run ID is not the current run.</p>
        <p>If any matching records exist, the Teams post is skipped. The error record is <strong>still created in Dataverse</strong> in all cases — every failure is logged regardless of throttle state.</p>
        <p>Setting <code>ppmf_AlertThrottleMinutes</code> to <code>0</code> causes the cutoff to equal the current time, meaning no prior records can fall within the window. Every failure will generate an alert.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Data Retention ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="card doc-section" id="retention">
      <div class="card-header">
        <span class="card-header-icon">🗑️</span>
        <div>
          <div class="card-title">Data Retention</div>
          <div class="card-subtitle">Automatic cleanup of resolved error records</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card-body prose">
        <p>The <strong>PPMF-Delete-Old-Errors</strong> flow runs every Sunday at midnight UTC. It deletes <code>ppmf_errorevent</code> records that meet <strong>all three</strong> criteria simultaneously:</p>
        <ol style="margin:8px 0 12px 20px;font-size:13px;color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.8">
          <li>Triage status is <em>Fixed</em>, <em>Duplicate</em>, <em>Won't Fix</em>, or <em>Closed</em></li>
          <li>Occurrence date is older than <code>ppmf_RetentionDays</code> days</li>
          <li>Record exists in the <code>ppmf_errorevent</code> table</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Records with status <em>New</em> or <em>In Progress</em> are never deleted. Setting <code>ppmf_RetentionDays</code> to <code>0</code> disables automatic deletion entirely. The flow can also be triggered manually on demand from the Power Automate portal.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Canvas App Errors ──────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="card doc-section" id="canvas-apps">
      <div class="card-header">
        <span class="card-header-icon">📱</span>
        <div>
          <div class="card-title">Canvas App Error Handling</div>
          <div class="card-subtitle">Sending app errors to PPMF from a Canvas App</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card-body prose">
        <p>Call <strong>PPMF-Power-Apps-Error-Handler-JSON</strong> from your canvas app using a Power Automate connection. The flow accepts a single <code>ErrorPayload</code> text parameter — a JSON string with the following fields:</p>

        <div class="code-block">
{
  <span class="str">"solutionName"</span>:  <span class="str">"YourSolutionName"</span>,
  <span class="str">"appname"</span>:       <span class="str">"Application display name"</span>,
  <span class="str">"appversion"</span>:    <span class="str">"1.0.0"</span>,
  <span class="str">"environment"</span>:   <span class="str">"Production"</span>,
  <span class="str">"sessionid"</span>:     <span class="str">"@{User().Email}-session"</span>,
  <span class="str">"username"</span>:      <span class="str">"Display Name"</span>,
  <span class="str">"useremail"</span>:     <span class="str">"user@domain.com"</span>,
  <span class="str">"activescreen"</span>:  <span class="str">"ScreenName"</span>,
  <span class="str">"errormessage"</span>:  <span class="str">"Error text"</span>,
  <span class="str">"errorsource"</span>:   <span class="str">"ControlName.Property"</span>,
  <span class="str">"severity"</span>:      <span class="str">"Warning"</span>
}
        </div>

        <p class="prose" style="margin-top:16px;margin-bottom:16px"><strong>How the error is processed</strong> — once the payload is received, the flow executes the following steps in sequence:</p>
        <div class="flow-diagram">
          <div class="flow-node">
            <span class="flow-node-icon">📱</span>
            <div>
              <div class="flow-node-name">Canvas App (OnError / custom handler)</div>
              <div class="flow-node-desc">Calls PPMF-Power-Apps-Error-Handler-JSON with a JSON-serialized ErrorPayload string</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
          <div class="flow-node">
            <span class="flow-node-icon">🔍</span>
            <div>
              <div class="flow-node-name">Alert Route Lookup</div>
              <div class="flow-node-desc">Queries ppmf_alertroutes for a matching active route; falls back to ppmf_TeamID and ppmf_FlowAlertsChannelID env vars if no match is found</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
          <div class="flow-node">
            <span class="flow-node-icon">⏱️</span>
            <div>
              <div class="flow-node-name">Throttle Check</div>
              <div class="flow-node-desc">Queries ppmf_errorevents for a recent record matching the same app and solution within the ppmf_AlertThrottleMinutes window</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
          <div class="flow-node">
            <span class="flow-node-icon">💬</span>
            <div>
              <div class="flow-node-name">Teams Alert Card (conditional)</div>
              <div class="flow-node-desc">Posted to the default channel (ppmf_TeamID / ppmf_FlowAlertsChannelID) only when no matching error was logged within the throttle window</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
          <div class="flow-node">
            <span class="flow-node-icon">💾</span>
            <div>
              <div class="flow-node-name">PPMF-Child-FlowWritetoIntakeList</div>
              <div class="flow-node-desc">Creates a ppmf_errorevent record in Dataverse — always runs regardless of throttle state</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="callout callout-info" style="margin-top:16px">
          <span class="callout-icon">ℹ️</span>
          <div><strong>Difference from the flow error path:</strong> Alert route lookup runs and resolves a matching route, but the Teams card is posted to the default channel from the environment variables regardless of the match. Per-solution channel routing is not applied to canvas app alerts. All other behaviour — throttle suppression and Dataverse logging — is consistent with the flow error path.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Security & Access Control ─────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="card doc-section" id="security">
      <div class="card-header">
        <span class="card-header-icon">🔐</span>
        <div>
          <div class="card-title">Security &amp; Access Control</div>
