            <tr>
              <td><span class="field-label">PPMF - Admin</span></td>
              <td><span class="field-desc">Power Platform administrators and solution owners responsible for framework setup and ongoing configuration.</span></td>
              <td><span class="field-desc">Full Create/Read/Write/Delete/Append/Append To/Assign/Share at Organization level on <code>ppmf_ErrorEvent</code>, <code>ppmf_ErrorNote</code>, and <code>ppmf_AlertRoute</code>.</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><span class="field-label">PPMF - Triager</span></td>
              <td><span class="field-desc">Support analysts and developers responsible for investigating, updating, and resolving errors.</span></td>
              <td><span class="field-desc"><code>ppmf_ErrorEvent</code>: Read/Write (Org), Append To (Org). <code>ppmf_ErrorNote</code>: Create/Read/Write/Delete/Append (User), Read (Org). <code>ppmf_AlertRoute</code>: Read (Org) only. Cannot modify Alert Routes.</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><span class="field-label">PPMF - Reader</span></td>
              <td><span class="field-desc">Stakeholders and auditors who need visibility into error events without the ability to modify records.</span></td>
              <td><span class="field-desc">Read-only access to <code>ppmf_ErrorEvent</code> (Org), <code>ppmf_ErrorNote</code> (Org), and <code>ppmf_AlertRoute</code> (Org). No create, write, or delete privileges on any PPMF table.</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><span class="field-label">PPMF - Service Account</span></td>
              <td><span class="field-desc">The application user created for the PPMF automation flows. Do not assign to human users.</span></td>
              <td><span class="field-desc"><code>ppmf_ErrorEvent</code>: Create/Read (Org), Append To (Org). <code>ppmf_ErrorNote</code>: Create (Org), Append (Org). <code>ppmf_AlertRoute</code>: Read (Org) only. Minimum privileges for the flow service principal.</span></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <div style="padding:20px">
          <div class="callout callout-warning">
            <span class="callout-icon">⚠️</span>
            <div>The <strong>PPMF - Service Account</strong> role is intended exclusively for the Power Automate application user. Assigning it to human users will prevent them from accessing the PPMF Platform Monitor app.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="callout callout-info" style="margin-top:8px">
            <span class="callout-icon">ℹ️</span>
            <div>All roles apply to <strong>Users and Teams</strong> except <strong>Service Account</strong>, which applies to <strong>Users</strong> only. Assign roles from the environment's <strong>Settings → Users + Permissions → Security Roles</strong>.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

